  "context": [
    "The Innova HyCross launched in January 2023 on an all-new monocoque platform derived from Toyota's TNGA-C architecture, a fundamental shift from the body-on-frame construction of the Innova Crysta it was positioned to eventually replace in retail sales. Toyota offers it with a 2.0-litre petrol engine paired to a CVT, and a 2.0-litre strong-hybrid powertrain paired to an e-CVT that combines the petrol engine with an electric motor without any plug-in charging requirement.",
    "A diesel option sits alongside the petrol and hybrid on the base G-SLF trim, aimed at buyers who put on heavy highway mileage and want the running-cost advantage, though it is a minority of the lineup next to the strong-hybrid's fuel-efficiency pitch.",
    "Toyota's hybrid powertrain, shared in concept with the Camry and Hyryder, has built an exceptionally strong reliability reputation among Indian owners for its fuel efficiency and low long-term running costs. That reputation, combined with waiting periods that have at times stretched to many months for hybrid variants, has pushed used HyCross hybrid prices unusually close to on-road prices shortly after a sale, a pattern rarely seen elsewhere in the mainstream MPV segment.",
    "Because the Innova Crysta continues to be sold separately for fleet and taxi use with its older diesel engine, the HyCross has effectively taken over the retail, family-buyer segment of the Innova franchise. This has let the HyCross build its own distinct resale identity relatively quickly, with hybrid variants trading at a consistent premium over petrol and CNG across every city tracked."
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "What is the resale value of a Toyota Innova HyCross in India?",
      "a": "A well-maintained HyCross retains roughly 84% of its ex-showroom price after two years, 78% after three years, and 67% after five years, as of September 2026, among the strongest retention of any mainstream vehicle in India. For a 2023 hybrid VX with 10,000-25,000 km, the current fair-market band is approximately ₹19.48–22.41 lakh."
    },
    {
      "q": "Does the HyCross hybrid hold value better than the petrol version?",
      "a": "Yes, by a wide margin. Across every year and km band in current data, the hybrid variants trade roughly 45% above the equivalent petrol variants, reflecting the hybrid's fuel-efficiency reputation and persistently long waiting periods for new units."
    },
    {
      "q": "Does the HyCross diesel hold its value as well as the hybrid?",
      "a": "No — the diesel trades below both the petrol and hybrid variants, since most buyers drawn to the HyCross specifically want the strong-hybrid's fuel-efficiency story, leaving the diesel a smaller, more price-sensitive segment of the used market."
    },
    {
      "q": "How much does an Innova HyCross depreciate per year?",
      "a": "The HyCross depreciates only about 9% in year one and a further 7% in year two, then settles into a steady 3-4% annual decline through year five. Ten-year retention of around 46% is roughly 22 points above the broader MPV segment average of 24%."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which city gives the best resale price for a HyCross?",
      "a": "Mumbai and Bengaluru currently trade at +3% above the national mid, driven by strong demand for hybrid variants among cab-aggregator and premium-MPV buyers. Kolkata trades at around -2%, where MPV resale cycles run longer."
    }
  ],
